msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/reproducible-builds.rst:104
msgid ""
"Reproducibility builds the target list twice. The first build will be run"
" using :ref:`Shared State <overview-manual/concepts:Shared State>` if "
"available, the second build explicitly disables :ref:`Shared State "
"<overview-manual/concepts:Shared State>` except for recipes defined in "
"the :term:`OEQA_REPRODUCIBLE_TEST_SSTATE_TARGETS` variable, and builds on"
" the specific host the build is running on. This means we can test "
"reproducibility builds between different host distributions over time on "
"the Autobuilder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/reproducible-builds.rst:112
msgid ""
"If ``OEQA_DEBUGGING_SAVED_OUTPUT`` is set, any differing packages will be"
" saved here. The test is also able to run the ``diffoscope`` command on "
"the output to generate HTML files showing the differences between the "
"packages, to aid debugging. On the Autobuilder, these appear under "
"https://valkyrie.yocto.io/pub/repro-fail/ in the form ``oe-reproducible +"
" <date> + <random ID>``, e.g. ``oe-reproducible-20200202-1lm8o1th``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/reproducible-builds.rst:119
msgid ""
"The project's current reproducibility status can be seen at :yocto_home"
":`/reproducible-build-results/`"
