#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:482
msgid ""
"*hasPackage(pkg):* Returns \"True\" if ``pkg`` is in the installed "
"package list of the image, which is based on the manifest file that is "
"generated during the :ref:`ref-tasks-rootfs` task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:486
msgid ""
"*hasFeature(feature):* Returns \"True\" if the feature is in "
":term:`IMAGE_FEATURES` or :term:`DISTRO_FEATURES`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:491
msgid "Class Attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:493
msgid "Class attributes are as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:495
msgid ""
"*pscmd:* Equals \"ps -ef\" if ``procps`` is installed in the image. "
"Otherwise, ``pscmd`` equals \"ps\" (busybox)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:498
msgid ""
"*tc:* The called test context, which gives access to the following "
"attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:501
msgid ""
"*d:* The BitBake datastore, which allows you to use stuff such as "
"``oeRuntimeTest.tc.d.getVar(\"VIRTUAL-RUNTIME_init_manager\")``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:504
msgid ""
"*testslist and testsrequired:* Used internally. The tests do not need "
"these."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:507
msgid ""
"*filesdir:* The absolute path to ``meta/lib/oeqa/runtime/files``, which "
"contains helper files for tests meant for copying on the target such as "
"small files written in C for compilation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:512
msgid ""
"*target:* The target controller object used to deploy and start an image "
"on a particular target (e.g. Qemu, SimpleRemote, and SystemdbootTarget). "
"Tests usually use the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:516
msgid "*ip:* The target's IP address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:518
msgid ""
"*server_ip:* The host's IP address, which is usually used by the DNF test"
" suite."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:521
msgid ""
"*run(cmd, timeout=None):* The single, most used method. This command is a"
" wrapper for: ``ssh root@host \"cmd\"``. The command returns a tuple: "
"(status, output), which are what their names imply - the return code of "
"\"cmd\" and whatever output it produces. The optional timeout argument "
"represents the number of seconds the test should wait for \"cmd\" to "
"return. If the argument is \"None\", the test uses the default instance's"
" timeout period, which is 300 seconds. If the argument is \"0\", the test"
" runs until the command returns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:531
msgid "*copy_to(localpath, remotepath):* ``scp localpath root@ip:remotepath``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:534
msgid ""
"*copy_from(remotepath, localpath):* ``scp root@host:remotepath "
"localpath``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:538
msgid "Instance Attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:540
msgid ""
"There is a single instance attribute, which is ``target``. The ``target``"
" instance attribute is identical to the class attribute of the same name,"
" which is described in the previous section. This attribute exists as "
"both an instance and class attribute so tests can use "
"``self.target.run(cmd)`` in instance methods instead of "
"``oeRuntimeTest.tc.target.run(cmd)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:548
msgid "Installing Packages in the DUT Without the Package Manager"
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:550
msgid ""
"When a test requires a package built by BitBake, it is possible to "
"install that package. Installing the package does not require a package "
"manager be installed in the device under test (DUT). It does, however, "
"require an SSH connection and the target must be using the ``sshcontrol``"
" class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:558
msgid ""
"This method uses ``scp`` to copy files from the host to the target, which"
" causes permissions and special attributes to be lost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:561
msgid ""
"A JSON file is used to define the packages needed by a test. This file "
"must be in the same path as the file used to define the tests. "
"Furthermore, the filename must map directly to the test module name with "
"a ``.json`` extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:566
msgid ""
"The JSON file must include an object with the test name as keys of an "
"object or an array. This object (or array of objects) uses the following "
"data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:570
msgid ""
"\"pkg\" --- a mandatory string that is the name of the package to be "
"installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:573
msgid ""
"\"rm\" --- an optional boolean, which defaults to \"false\", that "
"specifies to remove the package after the test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:576
msgid ""
"\"extract\" --- an optional boolean, which defaults to \"false\", that "
"specifies if the package must be extracted from the package format. When "
"set to \"true\", the package is not automatically installed into the DUT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/runtime-testing.rst:581
msgid ""
"Here is an example JSON file that handles test \"foo\" installing package"
" \"bar\" and test \"foobar\" installing packages \"foo\" and \"bar\". "
"Once the test is complete, the packages are removed from the DUT::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/test-process.rst:5
msgid "Project Testing and Release Process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/test-process.rst:8
msgid "Day to Day Development"
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/test-process.rst:10
msgid ""
"This section details how the project tests changes, through automation on"
" the Autobuilder or with the assistance of QA teams, through to making "
"releases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/test-process.rst:14
msgid ""
"The project aims to test changes against our test matrix before those "
"changes are merged into the master branch. As such, changes are queued up"
" in batches either in the ``master-next`` branch in the main trees, or in"
" user trees such as ``ross/mut`` in ``poky-contrib`` (Ross Burton helps "
"review and test patches and this is his testing tree)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/test-process.rst:20
msgid ""
"We have two broad categories of test builds, including \"full\" and "
"\"quick\". On the Autobuilder, these can be seen as \"a-quick\" and "
"\"a-full\", simply for ease of sorting in the UI. Use our Autobuilder "
":yocto_ab:`console view </valkyrie/#/console>` to see where we manage "
"most test-related items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/test-process.rst:26
msgid ""
"Builds are triggered manually when the test branches are ready. The "
"builds are monitored by the SWAT team. For additional information, see "
":yocto_wiki:`/Yocto_Build_Failure_Swat_Team`. If successful, the changes "
"would usually be merged to the ``master`` branch. If not successful, "
"someone would respond to the changes on the mailing list explaining that "
"there was a failure in testing. The choice of quick or full would depend "
"on the type of changes and the speed with which the result was required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/test-process.rst:35
msgid ""
"The Autobuilder does build the ``master`` branch once daily for several "
"reasons, in particular, to ensure the current ``master`` branch does "
"build, but also to keep (:yocto_git:`yocto-testresults </yocto-"
"testresults/>`), (:yocto_git:`buildhistory </poky-buildhistory/>`), and "
"our sstate up to date. On the weekend, there is a ``master-next`` build "
"instead to ensure the test results are updated for the less frequently "
"run targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/test-process.rst:43
msgid ""
"Performance builds (``buildperf-\\*`` targets in the console) are "
"triggered separately every six hours and automatically push their results"
" to the :yocto_git:`buildstats </yocto-buildstats/>` repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/test-process.rst:47
msgid ""
"The \"quick\" targets have been selected to be the ones which catch the "
"most failures or give the most valuable data. We run \"fast\" ptests in "
"this case for example but not the ones which take a long time. The quick "
"target doesn't include ``\\*-lsb`` builds for all architectures, some "
"``world`` builds and doesn't trigger performance tests or ``ltp`` "
"testing. The full build includes all these things and is slower but more "
"comprehensive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/test-process.rst:55
msgid "Release Builds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/test-process.rst:57
msgid ""
"The project typically has two major releases a year with a six month "
"cadence in April and October. Between these there would be a number of "
"milestone releases (usually four) with the final one being stabilization "
"only along with point releases of our stable branches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/test-process.rst:62
msgid ""
"The build and release process for these project releases is similar to "
"that in :ref:`test-manual/test-process:day to day development`, in that "
"the a-full target of the Autobuilder is used but in addition the form is "
"configured to generate and publish artifacts and the milestone number, "
"version, release candidate number and other information is entered. The "
"box to \"generate an email to QA\" is also checked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/test-process.rst:69
msgid ""
"When the build completes, an email is sent out using the ``send-qa-"
"email`` script in the :yocto_git:`yocto-autobuilder-helper </yocto-"
"autobuilder-helper>` repository to the list of people configured for that"
" release. Release builds are placed into a directory in "
"https://valkyrie.yocto.io/pub/releases on the Autobuilder which is "
"included in the email. The process from here is more manual and control "
"is effectively passed to release engineering. The next steps include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/test-process.rst:77
msgid ""
"QA teams respond to the email saying which tests they plan to run and "
"when the results will be available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/test-process.rst:80
msgid ""
"QA teams run their tests and share their results in the :yocto_git"
":`yocto-testresults-contrib </yocto-testresults-contrib>` repository, "
"along with a summary of their findings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../test-manual/test-process.rst:84
msgid "Release engineering prepare the release as per their process."
msgstr ""

